      "side": 1,
      "message": "This style of testing where you hold everything in members makes things difficult to read generally because in each method you don\u0027t know what happened to that object before. It also makes it hard in the future to test with multiple of any of these – suppose we want a test with 2 networks, or 2 sockets, how do we do that ? We can\u0027t reuse any of your existing setup, we have to rewrite everything.\n\nPlease consider better locality. For example you could have a data class and have doStartNattKeepalive return all the objects it has set up for the use of callers, instead of doing this pass-by-member style of call.\n\nNote that some of these are even completely useless as members : mNetwork is only used as a local in `setUp()` (the compiler warns about that), and mFd could just be read in doStartNattKeepalive instead of setUp and be kept local.\n\nI\u0027m not saying that members don\u0027t have their uses, but I guess my essential message is : please don\u0027t use a member as a means to pass an argument between methods.",
